# Temporal Data Architecture

Before planning or changing database schemas, Supabase, synchronization,
Dexie/IndexedDB, offline behavior, lifecycle state, historical views,
statistics, streaks, backup/restore, media persistence, account switching, or
conflict handling, read the complete architecture decision:

- `docs/architecture/temporal-data-sync.md`

Treat that document as binding repository guidance. Do not introduce:

- Effective-dated definition versions or apply-from schedule UI
- Ordinary hard deletion of accepted user history
- Non-idempotent synchronization operations
- Conflicts or pending-data failures without an in-app review/recovery path
- Silent last-write-wins for journal text or other reviewable conflicts

Any intentional departure must update the architecture document and explain
the changed product tradeoff before implementation.
